<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janus of Cyprus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1375–<a href="/years/1432">1432</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Janus was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> from 1398 to 1432. Born while his father was a prisoner of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>, he tried without success to recover Famagusta from the Genoese. Cypriot raids provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barsbay">Barsbay</a>, whose army invaded in 1426, defeated Janus at Khirokitia and took him prisoner to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>. He was freed for a large ransom, and Cyprus became tributary to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/janus-of-cyprus.jpg" alt="Janus of Cyprus" width="302" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Rama · CC BY-SA 3.0 cz · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Janus_of_Cyprus_CharlotteVendome.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
